# run.log — 2026-10-15-area-l4-ledger-reader — ZERO requests, offline pass
#
# There is no per-request table here because no request was sent. The columns the
# repo's ledger format requires (seq / method / status / t_queued / t_sent / t_done)
# have zero rows to carry. What this file records instead is each tool invocation
# this pass made, its exit status, and what it read.
#
# 0 of a 0 cap. Methods: none (GET 0, OPTIONS 0, POST 0). Delay: >=2s rule, not
# applicable, 0 requests sent, so no inter-request gap exists to report.
#
# LINE COUNTS. Two rules, both stated because getting either wrong makes a counted
# file uncounted:
#   1. grep -c '' is used, not wc -l. wc -l on a capture with no trailing newline
#      reports one line fewer than was printed — that understated every count in
#      an earlier revision of this file.
#   2. Captures are 2>&1, so a count is stdout + stderr TOGETHER. Only self-test
#      writes to stderr in normal operation (one UNREADABLE line, by design: the
#      integration negative control proves the reader refuses, and it says so on
#      stderr). So self-test's line count is its stdout + 1.
#
# invocation                 exit  output lines  what it did
# -------------------------  ----  ------------  ----------------------------------------
