read-area-l.py schemas        0            37  K1 key-sets 10, K2 member fields 3 by ^ipro_hcp scan, K3 properties
read-area-l.py manifest       0             9  wrote manifest.tsv, precedence order
read-area-l.py census         0           264  8 ledgers -> census + the member-limit block, vs census-84.txt
read-area-l.py self-test      0            39  25 controls, decomposition below
sh dup-test.sh                0            64  non-duplicate test, all successors + the stale-pointer check
python3 kib-detector.py       0            53  RULES 1-3: the whole-KiB detector, RULE 2, the 3 limit cells

# self-test decomposition — the 25 checks, grouped so the groups SUM to the count
# the function prints. Round 2 of the verifier found an earlier revision of this
# line listing 7 groups that summed to 22 against a stated 25: three middle checks
# were uncounted (the three fixtures agreeing on the member COUNT, on the path and
# host, and NOT on the timestamp). In a pass whose subject IS counted arithmetic, a
# decomposition that does not sum is the defect this repo keeps paying for.
#
#     5  parses         one fixture per committed schema (A/B/C/D) + the control row
#     8  normalisation  status resolves to int; control row is not DATA; the 2 real-ledger
#                        s7 checks (raw == "200" finds 0 of 19, reader resolves 10 of 19);
#                        3 fixtures agree on COUNT; on path+host; NOT on the timestamp; and
#                        a row with no member field reads None, not 0
#     2  member-source  a 200 row supplies the count; a lone 502 supplies None, not 0
#     5  refuses        5 synthetic rows the reader must raise Unreadable on
#     3  exhaustiveness empty population derives {} not a verdict; an all-controls crawl
#                        yields no verdict; row arithmetic is an int comparison
#     2  integration    unreadable row in a real 40-row ledger: refuses to emit, and
#                        --allow-unreadable records it rather than dropping it
#   ----
#    25  total (5 + 8 + 2 + 5 + 3 + 2). read-area-l.py self-test prints '(25 checks,
#         counted by this function, not asserted)' — the number is derived in code, not
#         asserted here. `grep -c PASS` over its output returns 26, because the summary
#         line contains the word PASS; the 25 are the check() calls.
